# Banned-words patterns (one ERE per line; '#' and blank lines ignored).
# Adding a name/string here makes the pre-commit hook reject any commit
# that introduces it anywhere in the tracked tree. Used to keep private
# household details (IPs, hostnames, family member names) out of the public repo.
#
# Personal additions belong in `.banned-words.local` (gitignored) so the
# patterns themselves don't leak through the public repo.

192\.168\.
10\.0\.
homeassistant\.local
